Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-18-2000||02:44 PM||||I noticed that since I welded the cradle back together last year (where the a-arm connects to it) it seems to have noticeable toe in. Also, my car is very slow to respond to movements. I can turn the wheel, adn the car will follow 1 second later. Are these related? And is there a way I can measure it myself and adjust the alignment? Not in the mood to spend $70.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-18-2000||09:30 PM||||yes they could be related. no this isn't something you want to mess with unless you know exactly what's what. you can easily make the problems much worse.<P>best fix is replace the cradel, put in polly or solid cradel bushings while you're at it, then align.<P>If you buy/build something to hang the engine then swapping the cradel is relativly painless. separate the ball joint from the spindles, separate the motor/tranny mounts and exhaust from engine, then the cradel bolts. slid the new one under and reverse the process. leave the exhaust attached to the cradle till you get it out. By hangin the motor you eliminate dealing with linkages plumbing and electrical.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||11-19-2000||01:29 PM||||Well, maybe I'll just do some measuring and try to get a little less toe in on the left side. I remember reading somewhere how to do this (Fiero secrets?). As for the bushings, I just made myself some aluminum ones, so I'm good to go there..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
